<h3>Meet the 5 Specialized AI Agents:</h3>

<div class="agent-card">
    <div class="agent-title">🩹 Agent 0: The Self-Healing Agent (Error Recovery Specialist)</div>
    <p><strong>Everyday Analogy:</strong> Like an automatic spell-checker in Microsoft Word that instantly fixes small typos before the document is sent for printing.</p>
    <p><strong>Job:</strong> If a user forgets a colon (<code>:</code>) after an <code>if</code> statement or has bad indentation, this agent catches the exact line error, patches the code autonomously, and alerts the user: <em>"Detected and healed 1 syntax error on Line 4 before running analysis."</em></p>
</div>

<div class="agent-card">
    <div class="agent-title">🕵️ Agent 1: The Structural Inspector (AST & PDG Detective)</div>
    <p><strong>Everyday Analogy:</strong> Like a structural architect examining the blueprint of a building before renovation begins.</p>
    <p><strong>Job:</strong> Analyzes the code's skeleton using AST and builds a complete map of control and data dependencies (who passes what data to whom). It compiles this into a clean <em>Structural Dossier</em>.</p>
</div>

<div class="agent-card">
    <div class="agent-title">🌿 Agent 2: The Green Computing Auditor (Energy Inspector)</div>
    <p><strong>Everyday Analogy:</strong> Like an energy efficiency inspector rating household appliances with an Energy Star sticker.</p>
    <p><strong>Job:</strong> Evaluates the code against software sustainability metrics: checks for deeply nested loops ($O(N^2)$ or $O(N^3)$), unmemoized recursion, and repeated file access. It assigns a baseline Eco Score (e.g., 55/100) and details the exact bottlenecks.</p>
</div>

<div class="agent-card">
    <div class="agent-title">✍️ Agent 3: The Multi-Level Summarizer (Technical Communicator)</div>
    <p><strong>Everyday Analogy:</strong> Like a skilled journalist who can write a 1-sentence headline for a busy CEO, a detailed story for engineers, or technical documentation for a manual.</p>
    <p><strong>Job:</strong> Instead of producing just one sentence, it generates three selectable output tiers:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Executive Summary:</strong> Plain English, non-technical explanation.</li>
            <li><strong>Developer Walkthrough:</strong> Detailed explanation of algorithms, inputs, and outputs.</li>
            <li><strong>Auto-Docstring Generator:</strong> Ready-to-copy, standard Google/Sphinx format docstrings complete with parameter types and return descriptions.</li>
        </ul>
    </p>
</div>

<div class="agent-card">
    <div class="agent-title">⚡ Agent 4: The Autonomous Green Optimizer & Verifier (Senior Refactorer)</div>
    <p><strong>Everyday Analogy:</strong> Like an expert mechanic who doesn't just tell you your car engine is burning too much fuel, but actually tunes the engine, takes it on a test lap, and proves it now uses 50% less gas.</p>
    <p><strong>Job:</strong>
        <ol>
            <li>Reads Agent 2's audit warnings (e.g., nested loops).</li>
            <li>Rewrites the code into an optimized, green version (e.g., using sets, list comprehensions, or caching).</li>
            <li><strong>Autonomous Verification Loop:</strong> It runs its own rewritten code back through the AST parser and green profiler. If it caused a syntax error or failed to improve the Eco Score, it self-reflects, fixes the mistake, and re-tests.</li>
            <li>Once validated, it outputs the certified green code with a verified Eco-Score improvement (e.g., 55/100 &rarr; 94/100).</li>
        </ol>
    </p>
</div>

<hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #cbd5e1; margin: 25px 0;">

